        "original_id": "9448c09a-8826-558b-8a60-cc7f1ef8460d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sandy Fox, Tiggy, Mike Judge, Greg Daniels, Judy and Mary\n- Works: King of the Hill, \"Freckles,\" \"Sobakasu,\" \"Why,\" \"Ring A Ling,\" Rurouni Kenshin\n- Roles: voice actress, singer, dancer\n- Places: Denmark, Southeast Asia\n\nFacts:\n- Sandy Fox was born on July 13, 1963.\n- Sandy Fox is an American voice actress, singer, and dancer.\n- Tiggy released the song \"Ring A Ling\" in 1996.\n- King of the Hill is an American animated sitcom created by Mike Judge and Greg Daniels.\n- King of the Hill ran on Fox from January 12, 1997 to September 13, 2009.\n- \"Ring A Ling\" was a number-one hit in Denmark in 1997.\n- Sandy Fox has had numerous roles in animated cartoons, anime, and video games.\n- Tiggy is known for her remix of Sandy Fox's song \"Freckles.\"\n- \"Freckles\" was originally the English version of Judy and Mary's song \"Sobakasu\" from the anime Rurouni Kenshin.\n- Tiggy was also popular in parts of Southeast Asia with the song \"Why.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
